---
system: sys-16-parent-mobile-application
flow_id: ble-provisioning
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/16-parent-mobile-application#5-3-device-and-provisioning-system-02
actors: [ParentApp, BLEDevice, Gateway, DeviceService, Device]
apis:
  - POST /v1/devices/provision/start
  - POST /v1/devices/provision/local-ble-paired
  - POST /v1/device/bootstrap-token
  - POST /v1/claim/confirm
  - GET /v1/devices/provision/:provisioningAttemptId/status
  - POST /v1/devices/provision/complete
externals: [BLE]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - ble_permission_denied
  - ble_device_not_found
  - already_assigned
  - provision_not_ready
  - wifi_handshake_failed
  - device_status_poll_timeout
idempotency: provisioningAttemptId issued by /provision/start scopes the BLE session — /provision/complete uses {provisioningAttemptId, deviceId, childProfileId} and is guarded by attempt status
retry: caller-side BLE scan retries on permission/timeout — never auto-retry /provision/complete on 4xx
timeout: BLE handshake 30s — HTTP calls 10s — provisioning status poll up to 5 minutes (3s interval)
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. Wi-Fi credentials travel only from the phone to firmware over encrypted BluFi. Backend owns claim/auth state; ESP server starts only after Wi-Fi and claim bootstrap succeed.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant BLEDevice
    participant Gateway
    participant DeviceService
    participant Firmware
    participant Router
    participant ESPServer

    ParentApp->>ParentApp: request BLE and location permissions
    alt ble_permission_denied
        ParentApp-->>ParentApp: navigate to settings prompt — abort
    else permission granted
        ParentApp->>BLEDevice: scan for "TBot-XXXX" advert
        alt ble_device_not_found
            BLEDevice-->>ParentApp: scan timeout (30s) — retry prompt
        else device discovered
            BLEDevice-->>ParentApp: serial advert (e.g. TBT-2026-004217)
            ParentApp->>BLEDevice: connect and discover services and read serial char
            BLEDevice-->>ParentApp: serial confirmation
            ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/provision/start {serialNumber, appVersion, phonePlatform}
            Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
            alt already_assigned
                DeviceService-->>Gateway: 409 already_assigned
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
            else ready
                DeviceService-->>Gateway: 200 {provisioningAttemptId, deviceId, deviceStatus=provisioning}
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
                ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/device/bootstrap-token
                Gateway-->>ParentApp: one-time claim bootstrap token
                ParentApp->>BLEDevice: encrypted BluFi token + device id + SSID/password
                BLEDevice->>Firmware: deliver authenticated BluFi frames
                Firmware->>Router: join 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi
                Firmware-->>ParentApp: STA_CONN_SUCCESS or STA_CONN_FAIL
                alt wifi_handshake_failed
                    ParentApp-->>ParentApp: correct password and retry BluFi
                else STA_CONN_SUCCESS
                    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/provision/local-ble-paired
                    Firmware->>Gateway: claim confirm or authenticated provisioning status
                    Gateway->>DeviceService: validate bootstrap token and ownership
                    DeviceService-->>Firmware: device secret and runtime configuration
                    Firmware->>Gateway: heartbeat
                    Firmware->>ESPServer: authenticated runtime WebSocket
                end
                loop poll every 3s up to 5 minutes
                    ParentApp->>Gateway: GET /v1/devices/provision/:provisioningAttemptId/status
                    Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
                    DeviceService-->>Gateway: {status: started | ble_paired | device_authenticated | completed | failed | expired}
                    Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
                end
                alt status failed or expired or poll timeout
                    ParentApp-->>ParentApp: surface retry-Wi-Fi-credentials prompt
                else device_authenticated or completed
                    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/devices/provision/complete {provisioningAttemptId, deviceId, assignChildProfileId, displayName}
                    Gateway->>DeviceService: forward
                    alt provision_not_ready
                        DeviceService-->>Gateway: 409 not_ready
                        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
                    else completed
                        DeviceService-->>Gateway: 200 OK
                        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
                    end
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,Firmware: Wi-Fi password stays in mobile transient memory and encrypted BluFi/firmware join path. Backend and ESP server never receive it.
